From 21e4b4834894604aa34bf96d859bbe19d25efeaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:36:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] worker-drain: adopt pre-existing state dirs at
 install, stay a no-op off POSIX, resolve import aliases in the spawn scan

Review round 1 of this PR found four defects in the previous head.

Install over an existing core-update dir. The update fence creates
core-update under the account umask (0775 on worker nodes) long before the
first drain install, and the hardened readers refuse a group-writable state
dir. install_state left the mode alone, so activation would have refused every
spawn, cron run, MCP connect and shell hook on the node. install_state now
tightens the dir and the lease dir through their own descriptors when a
trusted uid owns them, and refuses loudly for a symlink, another type or a
foreign owner. The lease dir is checked on every lease count and acquire, so
an untrusted lease dir reads as unknown-state, never as zero leases.

Windows. load_activation evaluated os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, which do not
exist there, so every seam routed through admit raised AttributeError.
load_activation now returns None when fcntl is unavailable and the flags fall
back to 0 at import.

Source scan. The AST scan only matched the literal name subprocess, so
`import subprocess as _sp` and `from subprocess import Popen` were invisible
(cua_backend_session._cli_run_json, batch_runner). It now resolves module and
function aliases file-wide, counts popen_worker calls and @fenced entry points
as routed seams, and the required-seams test no longer passes by default:
tools/registry.py and gateway/session_worker_spawn.py are recorded in the
inventory as incomplete_seams with the reason, and a test fails once either
gains a spawn or the fence. The cua-driver CLI fallback now runs under a lease.

Census root. observe_leases read this process's policy root while admit writes
under the activated account's root; a root-run heartbeat could have counted an
unrelated dir. Both now use the same root.

Also reverts fixture/cache/plugin_hooks.json, a test-run artifact.

Still INCOMPLETE and named in the code: no producer writes the process
baseline (host_processes is never zero in production, so scale-in stays off);
the composed test uses stand-ins for the Board, registry and scaler until the
scaler fence exists; registry.dispatch, the gateway session worker, platform
adapters and web actions hold no drain lease; seven-table custody and GC/WAL
are excluded.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_worker_drain*.py and tests/tools/test_worker_drain*.py
103 passed; 45 files touching the changed modules 696 passed, 12 skipped;
scripts/check --base origin/main 21 checks ok.
